    "summary": "T8 qualifies complete failed/incomplete checkpoint and canonical CR envelopes before admission and accepted attribution, retaining remaining-task/32KiB diagnostic capacity and checking actual merged canonical bytes under the store queue. USER REQUIREMENT CHANGE in the current turn: 'why 4MB cap? make it configurable'. Implemented review.maxJsonBytes (4MiB default, positive safe integer, live config reads) consistently across all decoders/checkpoints/snapshots/response schemas/CR writes and capacity gates, registered settings catalog, documented operator use. A next attempt that cannot fit retained history refuses until the configured budget is raised; both-route integration tests show raising to8MiB admits it without rewriting old attempts. Production build passed; 28 focused tests passed. Broad config/task-review sweep:344 pass,1 pre-existing unrelated tools.convertEscalate role/settings mismatch (HEAD package.json declares role absent from HEAD taxonomy); neither file changed. No real ~/.insrc/config.json modified; tests isolate HOME under/tmp.",
